    "explanation": "Both sides' central claims are accepted, and they point the same way: the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee cannot stand. The anchor clause POL-NS-01 requires all four conditions, and each one fails. (a) The trip record (EV-TRIP-00615) has arrived_at null and started_at null — the platform logged no driver 'arrived' event at all. (b) The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00615) never puts the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius; his closest approach was 2,919.5 m, with 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes out of 73. (c) The longest qualifying in-geofence run is 0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum — a 300-second shortfall. (d) The trip was cancelled by the rider with reason code RIDER_CHANGED_MIND, which is not one of the three driver-side codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises. With no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before cancellation, POL-NS-02 entitles the rider to a full refund, and POL-NS-06 confirms it: a 0-second dwell against a 300-second minimum makes the cancellation fee unchargeable whether or not the rider was present. The rider's own device (EV-GPS-00615 rider_presence, 54 fixes, mean 10.6 m, maximum 14.6 m, all inside the 100 m STANDARD radius) shows she was at the pickup throughout. POL-NS-03 does not rescue the fee — its 400 m ceiling is not met, since the driver was never stationary at 2,919.5 m — so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises. The driver's own in-app message, 'not coming, cancel yourself' (EV-CHAT-00615, sent 06:00:40), and his statement that 'a better job came up and I took it' are accepted as admissions that the pickup was abandoned on the driver's side; they reinforce the failure of limb (d) and foreclose any rider no-show finding. On the driver's side, POL-NS-07 compensation is not engaged because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full; the anti-farming check does not trip either — no_show_terminations_30d is 3 (below the '4 or more' limb) and 3 divided by 88 completed_trips_30d is 0.034 (below the 0.08 rate limb) — so no driver compensation is withheld or payable. Escalation is not engaged: the trace is complete (100% coverage, 0-second maximum gap, 73 fixes at the expected 10 s cadence), the chat log's single message matches trip_record.chat_message_count of 1, and the SGD 6.00 charged reconciles with the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_PLUS vehicle-tier fee (SGD 6.00) under fee_schedule.resolution_rule — so no POL-NS-08 limb (a) to (d) fires and no POL-NS-09 trigger applies. No false-arrival referral arises under POL-NS-05(ii): that clause runs only off a trip-record 'arrived' event, and this trip has none, so there is no marker to record against the driver. EV-ADVIS-00615-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0; it carries no fact, and no part of this ruling rests on it. Result: the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, with no driver compensation."
