    "explanation": "The SGD 6.00 no-show fee charged to the rider is refunded in full.\n\nUnder POL-NS-01 a cancellation fee stands only if all four conditions hold, and on this record none does. (a) EV-TRIP-00615 shows arrived_at as null — the platform logged no driver arrival event. (b) EV-GPS-00615 places the driver's closest approach at 2,919.5 m from the pickup pin, with 0 of 73 fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, so POL-NS-02's proximity test is not met; POL-NS-02 states that where no qualifying in-radius fix exists in the 15 minutes before cancellation the rider is entitled to a full refund. (c) The required dwell for a STANDARD pickup is 300 seconds; the measured in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds, a shortfall of 300 seconds, which under POL-NS-06 makes the fee unchargeable whether or not the rider was present — and EV-GPS-00615's rider track in fact places her 10.6 m on average from the pin, well inside the 100 m radius. (d) The trip was cancelled by the rider with reason code RIDER_CHANGED_MIND, not terminated by the driver with any of the three driver-side codes POL-NS-01(d) names. The driver is right that the platform record puts the cancellation in the rider's hands — that is precisely why limb (d) fails. The driver's own in-app message 'not coming, cancel yourself' (EV-CHAT-00615) and his statement that a better job came up are consistent with this outcome.\n\nDriver compensation: POL-NS-07 applies only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not, so no compensation is payable. The anti-farming check does not trip in any event (no_show_terminations_30d of 3 is below the threshold of 4, and 3/88 = 0.034 is below 0.08).\n\nThe driver's point that POL-NS-04 cannot be run against him is accepted, but it does not affect the fee: the refund is decided under POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06, not POL-NS-04.\n\nNo false-arrival referral is issued. POL-NS-05 runs off an 'arrived' event in the trip record, and this trip has none, so the clause has no marker